{% set local_problem %}
<p>Rural New Market properties face downspout challenges that suburban homes don't. Without municipal storm drains, water has to go somewhere on your property. If downspouts are undersized or poorly positioned, that water ends up exactly where you don't want it.</p>

<p>Many older homes have original downspouts that were never adequate for North Alabama's rainfall. Others have systems that were fine when installed but can't handle water from additions or modified rooflines.</p>

<p>Proper downspout design moves water safely away from your foundation and deposits it where it can't cause problems — even without a storm drain to connect to.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Good downspout systems have adequate capacity, proper positioning, and effective extensions.</p>

<p>Capacity means enough downspouts, correctly sized. Positioning means placing them where water naturally collects. Extensions (or underground drains) carry water to safe discharge points.</p>

<p>For rural New Market properties, we design with your specific terrain in mind — working with your property's features rather than assuming municipal infrastructure.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been solving drainage problems in north Madison County for over 20 years. We understand rural properties without city drainage and design systems accordingly.</p>

<p>Our solutions work with your property, not against it.</p>
{% endset %}

